-- title:
--   Zariski-local quotient of a formal mathcal O_D-module by a subgroup ideal
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a Noetherian commutative ring $B$ in which $p$ is nilpotent, a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X$ over $B$ (a $2$-dimensional commutative formal group law $X.F$ together with a family $a \mapsto X.\mathrm{act}\,a$, indexed by $W(\mathbb F_{p^2})$, and an element $X.\mathrm{varpi}$, all pairs of two-variable power series that are endomorphisms of the law, with $\mathrm{act}$ multiplicative for composition and additive for $X.F$, $\mathrm{varpi}\circ\mathrm{varpi}=\mathrm{act}\,p$ and $\mathrm{varpi}\circ\mathrm{act}\,a=\mathrm{act}(\varphi a)\circ\mathrm{varpi}$), an ideal $I$ of $B[\![x_1,x_2]\!]$ and a natural number $h$. Assume: $B[\![x_1,x_2]\!]/I$ is a finite projective $B$-module whose fibre dimension over $\kappa$ is $p^h$ for every field $\kappa$ and every ring homomorphism $B\to\kappa$ (after pushing $I$ forward coefficientwise); $x_i^q\in I$ for some $q$ and both $i$; every element of $I$ has vanishing constant term; substituting $X.F$ into an element of $I$ lands in the ideal generated by the two copies of $I$ in the four variables; and $I$ is stable under substitution of $X.\mathrm{act}\,a$ for all $a$ and of $X.\mathrm{varpi}$. Then there are finitely many $g_1,\dots,g_n\in B$ generating the unit ideal such that over each $B[1/g_i]$ there exist a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $Y$ and a pair $\rho$ of two-variable power series which is a homomorphism of laws commuting with the $\mathcal O_D$-action and with $\mathrm{varpi}$, whose kernel algebra is finite projective over $B[1/g_i]$ of fibre rank $p^h$, and with $(\rho_1,\rho_2)$ equal to the ideal generated by the image of $I$ in $B[1/g_i][\![x_1,x_2]\!]$.
--
--   This is the construction, in the formal $\mathcal O_D$-module setting, of the quotient of a formal group law by a finite locally free infinitesimal subgroup: Zariski-locally on the base the quotient is again a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module law and the quotient map is an $\mathcal O_D$-isogeny of height $h$ with kernel ideal exactly $I$. It feeds the construction of the moduli scheme of $\mathcal O_D$-stable subgroups of the special formal module used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_FormalODModule_exists_cover_isIsogenyOfHeight_span_range_eq_map_of_subgroup_ideal.lean

